# Questing Beast: "Combat damage that would be dealt by creatures you control can't be prevented." Bot1 attacks with
# Questing Beast and Llanowar Elves; Bot2 blocks the Elves with its own Llanowar Elves and casts Fog. Damage that can't be
# prevented is dealt anyway (CR 615.12): the Beast's 4 reaches Bot2, and Bot1's Elves deal their 1 to Bot2's Elves, which
# die. The combat damage of Bot2's Elves is Bot2's creature's, which the Beast says nothing about, so Fog prevents it and
# Bot1's Elves live: the one prevention recorded.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Forest
Mox Emerald
Questing Beast
Llanowar Elves
Island
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Fog
Island x25

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Questing Beast.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Questing Beast > Bot2; Llanowar Elves > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Llanowar Elves > Llanowar Elves)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Fog.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 16
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Damage = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves; Fog
Prevented = 1 Llanowar Elves > Llanowar Elves by Fog
